WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.340
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.610 --> 01:34.940
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.330 --> 01:37.840
[Episode 11]

4
01:38.710 --> 01:40.610
[Northern Guangxi Mountainous Area]

5
01:40.130 --> 01:41.090
Bo Gu.

6
01:40.740 --> 01:42.600
[Bo Gu (Qin Bangxian), Head of the CPC Central Committee]

7
01:41.259 --> 01:43.220
Comrade Bo Gu, I can walk.

8
01:43.390 --> 01:44.590
Tell them to halt.

9
01:44.590 --> 01:45.590
Halt here.

10
01:47.060 --> 01:48.460
I don't need a stretcher.

11
01:49.110 --> 01:50.509
I don't need a stretcher.

12
01:50.780 --> 01:51.750
Here, careful.

13
01:53.550 --> 01:54.500
Careful.

14
01:55.030 --> 01:56.190
Here.

15
01:59.700 --> 02:00.700
I don't need a stretcher.

16
02:00.700 --> 02:01.500
You go on ahead.

17
02:01.500 --> 02:03.360
Give it to them. They need it more.

18
02:03.830 --> 02:04.950
Comrade Bo Gu,

19
02:04.950 --> 02:07.590
I've been studying the Soviet-Russian War.

20
02:08.150 --> 02:11.660
There is much we can draw upon.

21
02:12.540 --> 02:14.310
The Defense of Tsaritsyn

22
02:14.910 --> 02:16.660
and the Buguruslan Operation,

23
02:17.500 --> 02:18.750
these campaigns

24
02:18.750 --> 02:20.780
offer many valuable lessons for us.

25
02:20.780 --> 02:21.780
Did you know?

26
02:22.060 --> 02:22.660
During these battles,

27
02:22.660 --> 02:24.310
the Soviet Red Army soldiers

28
02:24.910 --> 02:28.510
executed their commanders' strategic intentions flawlessly.

29
02:28.870 --> 02:30.200
What are your thoughts?

30
02:30.470 --> 02:31.910
Comrade Li De,

31
02:32.560 --> 02:34.620
[Li De, Military Adviser of the Communist International]

32
02:32.710 --> 02:34.829
let's discuss this once your fever breaks.

33
02:34.829 --> 02:36.600
I'm fine, Comrade Bo Gu.

34
02:37.620 --> 02:41.340
I believe we truly must draw upon

35
02:41.780 --> 02:43.820
the triumphant experiences of the Soviet Red Army.

36
02:43.820 --> 02:46.220
Commander-in-Chief, Comrade Zhou Enlai.

37
02:46.620 --> 02:47.660
Comrades,

38
02:47.660 --> 02:48.500
we must establish contact

39
02:48.500 --> 02:50.150
with the Comintern immediately.

40
02:49.570 --> 02:51.560
[Wu Xiuquan, Translator]

41
02:50.190 --> 02:50.820
We must establish contact

42
02:50.820 --> 02:52.220
with the Comintern immediately.

43
02:52.220 --> 02:53.780
We have been out of touch with them for far too long.

44
02:53.720 --> 02:55.670
[Zhou Enlai, CPC Central Committee Politburo Standing Committee, Vice-Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission, General Political Commissar of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

45
02:53.940 --> 02:56.740
We have been out of touch with them for far too long.

46
02:57.060 --> 02:58.430
Comrade Wu Xiuquan,

47
02:59.030 --> 03:00.150
tell Comrade Li De,

48
03:00.480 --> 03:02.570
the high-power radio we used to contact the Comintern

49
03:02.130 --> 03:05.750
[Zhu De, Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission (CRMC); Commander-in-Chief of the Red Army]

50
03:02.590 --> 03:03.820
via Shanghai

51
03:04.820 --> 03:06.350
was lost in the Xiang River.

52
03:06.470 --> 03:07.470
Comrade Li De,

53
03:07.470 --> 03:09.310
the high-power radio

54
03:09.310 --> 03:10.570
we used to contact the Comintern

55
03:10.570 --> 03:12.980
was lost in the Xiang River.

56
03:16.220 --> 03:17.540
Is this true?

57
03:24.060 --> 03:25.100
Careful!

58
03:26.150 --> 03:26.640
Stretcher!

59
03:26.640 --> 03:27.670
Here! Stretcher! Quick!

60
03:27.670 --> 03:28.780
Stretcher!

61
03:31.910 --> 03:32.660
Careful!

62
03:33.840 --> 03:35.400
Comrade Enlai.

63
03:38.190 --> 03:39.750
Let me handle this.

64
03:43.100 --> 03:44.270
Enlai.

65
03:45.870 --> 03:47.910
We can't let them keep running things into the ground.

66
03:47.910 --> 03:50.910
The troops are deeply dissatisfied with the command.

67
03:51.220 --> 03:52.280
If this continues,

68
03:52.430 --> 03:54.760
we'll lose the army's morale completely.

69
03:54.820 --> 03:55.550
Understood.

70
03:57.310 --> 04:00.370
We must restore Comrade Mao's voice in the leadership.

71
04:00.710 --> 04:02.270
That's all I needed to hear.

72
04:04.590 --> 04:11.600
[Ermu Cave, Bantang Village, Quanzhou, Guangxi]

73
04:05.660 --> 04:06.820
Peng Guangwen.

74
04:07.500 --> 04:08.500
Here.

75
04:10.270 --> 04:11.540
Huang Yimin.

76
04:12.600 --> 04:13.630
Here.

77
04:15.340 --> 04:16.740
Chen Bolin.

78
04:17.470 --> 04:18.149
Here.

79
04:19.540 --> 04:20.690
Li Ermao.

80
04:21.980 --> 04:22.420
Here.

81
04:23.780 --> 04:25.270
Wang Xing.

82
04:25.910 --> 04:26.740
Here.

83
04:27.540 --> 04:28.910
Xu Lishan.

84
04:29.980 --> 04:30.710
Here.

85
04:31.630 --> 04:33.100
Chen Feng.

86
04:37.030 --> 04:38.220
Chen Feng.

87
04:42.540 --> 04:43.980
Chen Feng.

88
05:02.420 --> 05:05.830
Chen was perfectly fine last night.

89
05:17.470 --> 05:19.740
We've completely blockaded the riverbank!

90
05:19.740 --> 05:20.910
There is no escape!

91
05:22.270 --> 05:24.630
If you step out and surrender right now,

92
05:24.910 --> 05:26.220
we have medical supplies

93
05:26.220 --> 05:27.830
and plenty of good food waiting for you!

94
05:27.830 --> 05:29.740
Once your wounds are treated and your bellies are full,

95
05:29.740 --> 05:31.150
we will send you all home!

96
05:33.100 --> 05:35.150
Let's charge out and fight them to the death!

97
05:35.150 --> 05:36.480
Fight them to the death!

98
05:39.030 --> 05:40.100
Comrades,

99
05:40.510 --> 05:41.980
regarding this matter,

100
05:42.590 --> 05:44.120
our company's Party branch

101
05:45.070 --> 05:47.300
has convened and discussed it.

102
05:48.060 --> 05:50.260
The Party branch has taken into account

103
05:50.270 --> 05:52.600
everyone's current physical condition,

104
05:53.420 --> 05:58.150
and determined that it's truly impossible for us to break out

105
05:58.980 --> 06:00.780
and catch up with the main force.

106
06:03.220 --> 06:05.820
However, our Xiang River Independent Company

107
06:06.220 --> 06:08.550
must never detach from the organization.

108
06:08.590 --> 06:10.150
We figured

109
06:10.540 --> 06:12.510
as long as our Independent Company

110
06:13.150 --> 06:16.860
has one comrade to break through

111
06:17.540 --> 06:19.340
and catch up with the main force,

112
06:19.340 --> 06:21.000
Command will know that

113
06:23.300 --> 06:26.160
the Xiang River Independent Company still exists.

114
06:26.420 --> 06:31.150
Whether we live or die,

115
06:31.860 --> 06:34.100
Command won't forget us.

116
06:35.540 --> 06:39.070
But we're all wounded now.

117
06:39.510 --> 06:41.180
Whoever breaks out

118
06:41.540 --> 06:44.340
won't last long.

119
06:51.659 --> 06:52.830
Xie,

120
06:53.070 --> 06:54.590
are you wounded?

121
06:57.710 --> 06:59.830
Just a few scratches.

122
07:01.910 --> 07:03.110
Will it slow you down?

123
07:03.220 --> 07:04.630
No.

124
07:06.830 --> 07:08.760
We're leaving this mission to you.

125
07:11.410 --> 07:12.330
Me?

126
07:13.220 --> 07:14.180
But...

127
07:14.390 --> 07:15.540
Xie,

128
07:16.070 --> 07:17.800
you're a martyr's descendant,

129
07:18.220 --> 07:21.270
and you're young.

130
07:21.950 --> 07:24.080
You won't draw the enemy's attention.

131
07:27.340 --> 07:28.220
Captain...

132
07:32.180 --> 07:33.340
Xie,

133
07:33.540 --> 07:35.510
you are a Red Army soldier now.

134
07:37.010 --> 07:38.570
That's an order.

135
07:46.510 --> 07:48.310
I swear to complete the mission!

136
07:48.340 --> 07:50.200
I will catch up with the main force

137
07:50.320 --> 07:53.530
and report our situation

138
07:55.220 --> 07:56.710
to Command!

139
07:59.270 --> 08:01.590
Captain, Instructor...

140
08:02.830 --> 08:04.150
When do I leave?

141
08:04.150 --> 08:05.420
As soon as it gets dark.

142
08:06.070 --> 08:07.710
The longer we wait, the more dangerous it gets.

143
08:07.710 --> 08:08.390
Yes, sir.

144
08:18.070 --> 08:19.390
This is

145
08:20.630 --> 08:22.950
our company's roster.

146
08:24.980 --> 08:28.220
It has the names of all the comrades

147
08:29.100 --> 08:31.270
in the Company,

148
08:32.460 --> 08:35.230
along with records of their original units,

149
08:37.419 --> 08:40.030
including those who laid down their lives.

150
08:42.630 --> 08:44.690
Once you catch up with the main force,

151
08:45.350 --> 08:47.060
hand this over to Command.

152
08:57.540 --> 09:00.110
Xie, here.

153
09:04.950 --> 09:06.660
Take this for the road.

154
09:09.870 --> 09:11.060
Kid,

155
09:15.340 --> 09:16.310
be careful.

156
09:28.580 --> 09:29.990
You keep it.

157
09:30.660 --> 09:33.030
I can forage for food out there.

158
09:33.540 --> 09:37.060
Eat it so you have the strength to cross the river.

159
09:38.030 --> 09:38.910
Eat.

160
09:43.540 --> 09:44.990
Eat.

161
09:45.780 --> 09:46.940
Eat up, Xie.

162
09:46.990 --> 09:48.470
You need your strength.

163
09:48.990 --> 09:50.820
This is from all of us.

164
09:51.030 --> 09:51.460
Right.

165
09:51.540 --> 09:52.460
Eat.

166
09:52.540 --> 09:52.990
Eat.

167
09:53.020 --> 09:54.020
Go on.

168
09:54.870 --> 09:56.270
Okay.

169
10:02.750 --> 10:03.990
Comrade Xingguo,

170
10:05.700 --> 10:06.990
if

171
10:07.940 --> 10:10.670
you run into our comrades from the 15th Division,

172
10:12.110 --> 10:13.580
tell them

173
10:15.940 --> 10:17.460
once my wounds heal,

174
10:19.180 --> 10:20.700
I'll find them.

175
10:31.070 --> 10:32.140
Drink some water.

176
10:32.780 --> 10:34.110
Don't choke.

177
10:49.060 --> 10:50.300
Xie.

178
10:52.270 --> 10:52.940
Captain.

179
10:53.350 --> 10:54.560
Put this on.

180
11:08.460 --> 11:09.540
Go.

181
11:40.660 --> 11:43.270
In 2018 and 2019,

182
11:44.060 --> 11:45.350
the Quanzhou County Government

183
11:45.350 --> 11:47.150
conducted two recovery and protection operations

184
11:47.150 --> 11:50.660
for the remains of Red Army soldiers from the Xiang River Campaign.

185
11:50.660 --> 11:51.990
In Ermu Cave alone,

186
11:51.990 --> 11:55.510
thirty complete remains

187
11:55.630 --> 11:57.990
and over 3,000 bone fragments were excavated.

188
11:57.990 --> 11:58.920
Local personnel

189
11:58.990 --> 12:00.990
discovered a complete skeleton

190
12:01.060 --> 12:03.420
near a cliff not far from the cave.

191
12:04.180 --> 12:06.040
He was leaning against the cliff,

192
12:06.200 --> 12:07.230
with one arm

193
12:07.300 --> 12:10.700
stretching toward a nearby blue-and-white porcelain bowl,

194
12:11.370 --> 12:13.780
less than 30 centimeters away.

195
12:14.030 --> 12:17.300
Based on skeletal development analysis and isotope dating,

196
12:17.300 --> 12:20.820
the bone age of these remains was determined to be under 14.

197
12:21.390 --> 12:23.270
This porcelain bowl is now housed in

198
12:23.270 --> 12:26.390
the Red Army Long March Xiang River Campaign Memorial

199
12:28.300 --> 12:35.940
[Laoshanjie, Guangxi]

200
12:40.830 --> 12:43.300
How much longer do we have to climb?

201
12:42.320 --> 12:45.460
[Wei Yueqiao, Staff Member of the Second Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

202
12:43.910 --> 12:45.980
According to the Yao villagers at the foot of the mountain,

203
12:45.980 --> 12:49.800
[Zeng Xisheng, Director of the Second Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

204
12:46.110 --> 12:47.380
it's 30 li up

205
12:47.540 --> 12:48.990
and 15 li down.

206
12:49.390 --> 12:51.390
There's a place ahead called Leigongyan,

207
12:51.390 --> 12:52.700
which is even steeper.

208
12:52.820 --> 12:53.820
Tell the comrades

209
12:53.820 --> 12:55.630
to push through and keep climbing.

210
12:55.630 --> 12:57.990
This must be the highest mountain we've scaled

211
12:57.990 --> 12:59.770
since our strategic relocation began.

212
12:59.770 --> 13:02.360
We'll likely have to spend the night on the mountain.

213
13:02.360 --> 13:03.690
The mountains are nice.

214
13:03.810 --> 13:05.810
The sky for a roof, the earth for a bed.

215
13:05.110 --> 13:06.680
[Cao Xiangren, Section Chief of the Second Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

216
13:07.270 --> 13:08.390
Watch your step.

217
13:14.000 --> 13:17.720
[Qian Zhuangfei, Deputy Director of the Second Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

218
13:15.750 --> 13:16.910
Careful now.

219
13:19.060 --> 13:20.540
Watch your step.

220
13:21.390 --> 13:21.750
Easy now.

221
13:21.750 --> 13:22.820
Watch your step, everyone.

222
13:22.820 --> 13:24.270
Watch your step.

223
13:24.630 --> 13:26.300
Find your footing before you step.

224
13:26.300 --> 13:27.570
Watch your step.

225
13:28.050 --> 13:29.850
Plant your feet before you step.

226
13:32.990 --> 13:34.580
Halt and rest!

227
13:35.180 --> 13:36.230
Take a break here!

228
13:48.270 --> 13:49.300
Qian.

229
13:49.700 --> 13:52.150
Give the boys some food for thought.

230
13:52.230 --> 13:53.180
Something to boost morale.

231
13:53.180 --> 13:54.390
Come on, Qian, give us a piece.

232
13:54.390 --> 13:56.030
Let's hear it! Let's hear it!

233
13:56.060 --> 13:57.900
Alright, I'll give you one.

234
14:03.820 --> 14:06.580
We are moving the earth.

235
14:07.780 --> 14:11.140
We have the fate of mankind.

236
14:12.870 --> 14:16.270
We are a group of people

237
14:16.480 --> 14:18.370
while singing high notes.

238
14:19.150 --> 14:22.060
Bravo! Bravo!

239
14:22.060 --> 14:24.180
This is the song

240
14:24.350 --> 14:25.510
who wrote "We".

241
14:25.510 --> 14:27.180
At it again, eh?

242
14:27.180 --> 14:28.110
Drink some.

243
14:28.420 --> 14:29.700
Currently,

244
14:30.060 --> 14:32.540
we're trapped in a black pit like hell.

245
14:33.820 --> 14:37.420
But we knew we were going to win.

246
14:37.750 --> 14:40.580
We work together step by step

247
14:41.060 --> 14:44.420
and get closer to our victory morning.

248
14:44.580 --> 14:49.230
Excellent!

249
14:49.910 --> 14:50.460
Bravo!

250
14:52.630 --> 14:54.350
Comrades, move out!

251
14:54.460 --> 14:55.770
Light the torches!

252
14:56.580 --> 14:57.790
Move out!

253
14:58.150 --> 14:58.680
Let's go!

254
14:58.810 --> 14:59.110
Move!

255
14:59.110 --> 14:59.850
We're moving out!

256
14:59.850 --> 15:00.880
Move out!

257
15:27.690 --> 15:28.500
Jiaxiang,

258
15:28.880 --> 15:31.290
I was thinking of Comrade Zedong's

259
15:31.780 --> 15:34.020
1930 article,

260
15:34.040 --> 15:35.230
titled Survey Work.

261
15:36.060 --> 15:39.750
Two points in it really struck me.

262
15:40.000 --> 15:42.890
[Luofu (Zhang Wentian), Member of the Political Bureau Standing Committee of the CPC Central Committee; Chairman of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

263
15:40.420 --> 15:41.490
First, it says

264
15:42.280 --> 15:43.920
we need books,

265
15:44.810 --> 15:45.960
but we must correct

266
15:45.990 --> 15:49.030
[Wang Jiaxiang, Vice-Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission; Director of the General Political Department of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

267
15:46.060 --> 15:48.460
the book worship that ignores reality.

268
15:48.870 --> 15:52.270
Second, it says the victory of the Chinese revolution

269
15:52.660 --> 15:56.940
relies on Chinese comrades understanding the situation in China.

270
15:57.250 --> 15:58.320
It's a shame.

271
15:58.580 --> 16:02.460
We put the Soviet Union's successful experience on a pedestal.

272
16:04.370 --> 16:05.650
Looking back now,

273
16:06.660 --> 16:09.920
from the Fifth Counter-Encirclement Campaign until now,

274
16:10.350 --> 16:11.990
our military command

275
16:12.300 --> 16:14.560
has suffered from precisely this issue.

276
16:14.630 --> 16:16.910
We handed military command and decision-making power

277
16:16.910 --> 16:18.270
entirely to Li De,

278
16:18.660 --> 16:20.330
who knows nothing

279
16:20.350 --> 16:21.870
of the reality in China.

280
16:22.230 --> 16:25.350
He took the so-called Soviet revolutionary experience

281
16:25.350 --> 16:27.060
and applied it blindly.

282
16:27.450 --> 16:27.990
And the result?

283
16:27.990 --> 16:29.730
We completely abandoned

284
16:29.750 --> 16:34.150
the successful experience of our first four Counter-Encirclement Campaign.

285
16:34.230 --> 16:35.540
It's a shame.

286
16:36.350 --> 16:37.630
It's a tragedy.

287
16:38.420 --> 16:42.380
Let's hope the massive setbacks we've suffered

288
16:43.000 --> 16:46.050
will trigger a great awakening.

289
16:46.420 --> 16:47.300
At the very least,

290
16:47.300 --> 16:50.060
it might make our leadership a bit wiser,

291
16:50.350 --> 16:51.790
so they can, as Lenin said,

292
16:51.790 --> 16:55.060
make a concrete analysis of concrete conditions.

293
17:05.180 --> 17:06.069
Xie, Chen,

294
17:06.180 --> 17:07.420
come on, set it down.

295
17:10.869 --> 17:11.630
Here.

296
17:12.940 --> 17:13.700
Here.

297
17:14.980 --> 17:15.550
Easy.

298
17:23.800 --> 17:27.420
[Mao Zedong, Chairman of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

299
17:49.110 --> 17:50.630
It seems we can't go back

300
17:52.180 --> 17:55.110
to the Central Soviet Area.

301
17:55.830 --> 17:58.910
What began as a planned strategic retreat

302
17:59.500 --> 18:02.550
has turned into a perilous,

303
18:02.940 --> 18:04.590
deadly expedition.

304
18:04.870 --> 18:06.910
Where does our path lie?

305
18:12.500 --> 18:14.220
We must find it,

306
18:16.350 --> 18:17.260
forge ahead,

307
18:20.630 --> 18:21.460
and walk it.

308
18:30.600 --> 18:38.140
[Shaanxi Geng River]

309
18:32.940 --> 18:35.660
As the Central Red Army crossed Laoshanjie

310
18:35.660 --> 18:38.020
and entered northern Guangxi,

311
18:38.260 --> 18:39.460
the 25th Red Army

312
18:39.590 --> 18:41.920
also began its arduous fighting retreat.

313
18:42.350 --> 18:44.910
On December 9, 1934,

314
18:45.070 --> 18:47.630
after a long trek, the 25th Red Army

315
18:47.630 --> 18:48.980
crossed the Mangling Mountains

316
18:48.980 --> 18:51.460
and entered Yujiahe in southern Shaanxi.

317
18:52.350 --> 18:53.660
On December 10,

318
18:53.870 --> 18:55.630
a meeting was held in Yujiahe

319
18:55.550 --> 18:59.820
[Xu Baoshan, Secretary of the CPC Hubei-Henan-Anhui Provincial Committee]

320
18:55.910 --> 18:58.350
to discuss the establishment of a new base area

321
18:58.350 --> 19:00.660
in the Hubei-Henan-Shaanxi border region.

322
18:59.980 --> 19:04.000
[Cheng Zihua, Commander of the 25th Red Army] [Xu Haidong, Deputy Commander of the 25th Red Army]

323
19:01.220 --> 19:02.350
During the meeting,

324
19:02.420 --> 19:05.220
they were ambushed by the Nationalist 60th Division.

325
19:04.170 --> 19:05.810
[Zheng Weisan, Secretary-General of the CPC Hubei-Henan-Anhui Provincial Committee]

326
19:05.790 --> 19:06.660
In the battle,

327
19:06.940 --> 19:08.310
Commander Cheng Zihua

328
19:08.310 --> 19:11.550
and Deputy Commander Xu Haidong were severely wounded.

329
19:20.150 --> 19:21.180
Director Qian!

330
19:21.550 --> 19:22.500
Director Qian!

331
19:22.700 --> 19:25.230
Quick! The commander is hit and unconscious.

332
19:25.330 --> 19:26.190
Where's he hit?

333
19:26.660 --> 19:29.220
A bullet went straight through both his hands.

334
19:29.220 --> 19:29.460
Quick!

335
19:29.460 --> 19:30.110
Gauze!

336
19:30.310 --> 19:30.660
Coming.

337
19:30.660 --> 19:32.660
His left wrist won't stop bleeding!

338
19:33.090 --> 19:35.000
[Qian Xinzhong, Director of the 25th Red Army Hospital]

339
19:37.660 --> 19:38.320
Commander!

340
19:38.350 --> 19:40.100
The artery in your left wrist is severed.

341
19:40.100 --> 19:41.420
Let me stop the bleeding first.

342
19:41.420 --> 19:42.350
Press down here.

343
19:42.940 --> 19:44.460
Hard! Press hard!

344
19:45.630 --> 19:46.620
Get some more gauze.

345
19:46.620 --> 19:47.550
Okay. Hurry.

346
19:48.070 --> 19:49.260
Don't let him drink too much water yet.

347
19:49.260 --> 19:50.460
Watch closely. Okay.

348
19:50.550 --> 19:51.410
Director Qian!

349
19:51.500 --> 19:52.430
Here! Over here!

350
19:52.940 --> 19:53.550
Make way!

351
19:53.580 --> 19:54.380
Make way!

352
19:54.630 --> 19:55.490
Director Qian!

353
19:56.910 --> 19:57.970
Deputy Commander!

354
19:58.310 --> 19:59.510
Deputy Commander Xu!

355
20:00.500 --> 20:02.390
The Deputy Commander took a bullet to the head!

356
20:02.390 --> 20:03.520
You have to save him!

357
20:03.830 --> 20:06.090
Deputy Commander Xu! Deputy Commander Xu!

358
20:06.090 --> 20:07.290
Deputy Commander Xu!

359
20:07.390 --> 20:08.590
Deputy Commander Xu!

360
20:09.340 --> 20:11.540
Do something, Director Qian! Save him!

361
20:13.480 --> 20:15.550
His airway is blocked by blood and phlegm.

362
20:15.550 --> 20:16.810
We need to clear it out.

363
20:16.870 --> 20:17.800
Then do it, hurry!

364
20:17.800 --> 20:18.700
We don't have suction equipment.

365
20:18.700 --> 20:19.870
I can't.

366
20:19.870 --> 20:21.350
Then figure something out!

367
20:21.350 --> 20:23.070
What are you even here for?

368
20:24.420 --> 20:26.070
The Deputy Commander cannot die!

369
20:26.070 --> 20:27.870
Do whatever it takes to save him!

370
20:27.940 --> 20:28.600
Find a tube.

371
20:28.720 --> 20:29.350
Go find a tube!

372
20:29.350 --> 20:29.870
Go find a tube!

373
20:29.870 --> 20:30.500
Yes, sir!

374
20:30.500 --> 20:32.020
You have to save him, whatever the cost!

375
20:32.020 --> 20:33.180
Find a tube! Hurry!

376
20:33.180 --> 20:34.660
Go! Find a tube!

377
20:34.740 --> 20:35.390
Hurry!

378
20:35.630 --> 20:37.740
Hold on, Deputy Commander Xu! Stay with us!

379
20:37.740 --> 20:38.870
Director Qian!

380
20:39.220 --> 20:40.070
Let me try.

381
20:40.100 --> 20:41.100
Hold on!

382
20:46.200 --> 20:48.970
[Zhou Shaolan, Nurse of 25th Red Army]

383
21:47.350 --> 21:48.480
His airway is clear.

384
21:48.590 --> 21:49.980
He'll live! He'll live!

385
21:50.040 --> 21:51.100
Deputy Commander!

386
21:53.600 --> 21:54.660
He pulled through!

387
21:58.870 --> 22:00.360
Bad news!

388
22:00.460 --> 22:02.060
The enemy is charging again!

389
22:03.460 --> 22:05.660
Director Qian, I'm leaving this to you.

390
22:06.260 --> 22:06.820
Come with me!

391
22:06.820 --> 22:07.740
Yes!

392
22:07.830 --> 22:08.700
Hold on!

393
22:08.740 --> 22:09.820
Hold on!

394
22:12.810 --> 22:14.020
Zhou!

395
22:16.080 --> 22:17.970
[Han Xianchu, Company Commander, 2nd Battalion, 225th Regiment, 25th Red Army]

396
22:21.580 --> 22:22.430
Follow me!

397
22:22.660 --> 22:23.350
Yes!

398
22:23.940 --> 22:24.540
Come here!

399
22:25.150 --> 22:26.310
Quick! Get the Deputy Commander inside.

400
22:26.310 --> 22:26.830
We operate immediately.

401
22:26.830 --> 22:27.310
-Hurry! -Yes!

402
22:27.310 --> 22:27.660
Yes!

403
22:27.830 --> 22:28.870
Hurry!

404
22:29.110 --> 22:31.110
You two, stitch up Commander!

405
22:31.550 --> 22:32.500
Move now!

406
22:32.790 --> 22:33.150
Quick!

407
22:33.150 --> 22:33.630
Easy.

408
22:33.740 --> 22:34.270
Let's go.

409
22:34.910 --> 22:36.460
Make way! Make way!

410
22:36.630 --> 22:37.830
Prepare for surgery.

411
22:48.570 --> 22:50.810
Under the command of Political Commissar Wu Huanxian,

412
22:50.810 --> 22:53.920
the 25th Red Army fought back bravely.

413
22:53.940 --> 22:56.110
After over twenty brutal countercharges

414
22:56.110 --> 22:57.220
lasting until dusk,

415
22:57.220 --> 22:59.220
they finally broke the enemy lines.

416
23:00.000 --> 23:02.470
From their departure on November 16th to this battle,

417
23:02.470 --> 23:04.070
in just over twenty days,

418
23:04.370 --> 23:07.260
the 25th Red Army marched over a thousand li,

419
23:07.290 --> 23:08.980
fighting almost every single day.

420
23:08.980 --> 23:10.840
With a force of less than 3000 men,

421
23:11.030 --> 23:12.420
they shattered the encirclements and blockades

422
23:12.420 --> 23:14.460
of an enemy force dozens of times their size,

423
23:14.460 --> 23:16.930
tenaciously carving out a passage to the west

424
23:16.930 --> 23:18.240
and successfully completing

425
23:18.240 --> 23:20.570
the first phase of strategic relocation.

426
23:49.980 --> 23:57.790
[West Bank of the Xiang River, Guangxi]

427
24:35.020 --> 24:35.680
Over there.

428
24:42.600 --> 24:43.420
Go check that sector.

429
24:43.420 --> 24:43.950
Yes, sir.

430
24:44.350 --> 24:45.680
The rest of you, with me.

431
25:12.790 --> 25:14.120
Let's check over there.

432
26:10.990 --> 26:23.650
[Body collectors are guilty as Communists. Execution on sight.]

433
29:18.850 --> 29:19.900
[A Brief Account of the Pacification of the Miao]

434
29:19.930 --> 29:23.830
[Tongdao, Hunan]

435
29:49.260 --> 29:52.150
It's so late now,

436
29:53.160 --> 29:54.960
but tomorrow's marching orders

437
29:54.990 --> 29:56.470
have yet to be issued.

438
29:56.870 --> 29:57.790
Word is

439
29:58.240 --> 30:00.320
Bo Gu and Li De are still insisting

440
30:00.500 --> 30:01.570
on heading north via Tongdao

441
30:01.570 --> 30:04.500
to link up with the 2nd and 6th Corps in western Hunan.

442
30:05.110 --> 30:06.590
I just don't understand.

443
30:07.110 --> 30:09.870
Did they even read the Second Bureau's intel report?

444
30:09.870 --> 30:11.800
The deployment orders from Liu Jianxu of the Hunan Army

445
30:11.800 --> 30:12.950
are crystal clear.

446
30:13.260 --> 30:15.460
There are multiple blockades in western Hunan

447
30:15.460 --> 30:17.500
just waiting for us to walk right into their trap.

448
30:17.500 --> 30:19.460
If they knew how to adapt,

449
30:19.460 --> 30:22.720
we wouldn't have suffered such a defeat at the Xiang River.

450
30:27.370 --> 30:29.900
I will say this one more time.

451
30:30.070 --> 30:34.940
The general direction of the Red Army's advance shall not change.

452
30:35.310 --> 30:36.220
Comrade Li De,

453
30:36.480 --> 30:39.910
according to the enemy cables intercepted by the Second Bureau,

454
30:39.910 --> 30:41.110
the Nationalist Army

455
30:41.180 --> 30:42.930
has already set up new blockades

456
30:42.930 --> 30:44.780
along our path north.

457
30:45.500 --> 30:49.020
Why must we force our way through?

458
30:50.350 --> 30:51.260
Zhu De,

459
30:51.390 --> 30:54.760
are you questioning my command?

460
30:55.870 --> 30:58.600
As Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission,

461
30:58.600 --> 31:02.080
do I lack even the right to question it?

462
31:03.310 --> 31:05.390
I will stress this again.

463
31:05.950 --> 31:08.310
The authority to decide on this strategic transfer

464
31:08.310 --> 31:09.460
rests with the Troika.

465
31:09.460 --> 31:10.500
The authority to decide on this strategic transfer

466
31:10.500 --> 31:11.760
rests with the Troika.

467
31:12.350 --> 31:14.110
Heading north to western Hunan

468
31:14.110 --> 31:16.310
was approved by the Comintern.

469
31:16.330 --> 31:19.850
We will make contact with the Comintern sooner or later.

470
31:22.070 --> 31:23.760
If you continue to command like this,

471
31:23.760 --> 31:25.740
there'll be no need to contact the Comintern.

472
31:25.740 --> 31:28.070
The Red Army will be completely wiped out.

473
31:28.150 --> 31:30.600
Was the disaster at the Xiang River not enough of a lesson?

474
31:30.600 --> 31:33.070
How many more such battles do you intend to command?

475
31:33.070 --> 31:36.270
How many more people can the Red Army afford to sacrifice?

476
31:38.460 --> 31:40.380
Zhu De, I understand.

477
31:40.460 --> 31:44.040
You must be under Mao Zedong's influence.

478
31:44.060 --> 31:45.060
I heard

479
31:45.490 --> 31:49.600
Mao Zedong, Luofu, and Wang Jiaxiang

480
31:50.150 --> 31:55.110
have been openly criticizing our command along the way.

481
31:55.460 --> 31:57.390
If our command is indeed flawed,

482
31:57.660 --> 32:00.070
why shouldn't we heed the criticism of others?

483
32:00.070 --> 32:01.870
If others have good suggestions,

484
32:01.870 --> 32:03.630
why can't we accept them?

485
32:03.650 --> 32:04.650
Comrade Li De,

486
32:04.790 --> 32:05.590
Comrade Bo Gu,

487
32:05.870 --> 32:07.500
given such critical military intelligence,

488
32:07.500 --> 32:09.740
we cannot afford to make decisions recklessly.

489
32:09.740 --> 32:12.790
I suggest we convene an emergency meeting.

490
32:13.180 --> 32:16.550
Let us discuss it collectively before making a decision.

491
32:17.700 --> 32:18.630
Zhou Enlai.

492
32:18.680 --> 32:22.140
Are we not discussing it now?

493
32:22.160 --> 32:25.490
Who else do you want to discuss it with?

494
32:26.070 --> 32:28.350
I think, at the very least,

495
32:28.910 --> 32:33.590
Comrade Mao Zedong should be invited to participate.

496
32:33.740 --> 32:35.940
I completely agree.

497
32:43.110 --> 32:44.240
Very well.

498
32:45.070 --> 32:46.310
Comrade Enlai,

499
32:46.790 --> 32:49.050
I leave it to you to convene this meeting.

500
32:49.290 --> 32:50.250
All right.

501
32:50.700 --> 32:52.350
I will invite Comrade Mao Zedong,

502
32:52.350 --> 32:53.350
Comrade Luofu,

503
32:53.590 --> 32:56.190
and Comrade Wang Jiaxiang to join the meeting.

504
33:02.900 --> 33:04.830
I will notify them now.

505
33:21.940 --> 33:22.790
Enlai.

506
33:23.960 --> 33:24.920
Commander.

507
33:25.390 --> 33:26.390
Enlai,

508
33:26.390 --> 33:28.660
you've taken a big step this time.

509
33:29.660 --> 33:32.380
It's time Mao was brought in from the cold.

510
33:32.790 --> 33:34.390
I have learned from our bitter lessons.

511
33:34.390 --> 33:35.350
Besides,

512
33:35.550 --> 33:38.010
Comrade Zedong is a member of the Politburo.

513
33:44.220 --> 33:45.590
The problem now is

514
33:45.740 --> 33:49.460
if we don't head north into Hunan,

515
33:49.790 --> 33:51.660
where do we go next?

516
33:56.910 --> 33:59.500
Continue west into Guizhou.

517
34:00.210 --> 34:01.010
Into Guizhou?

518
34:01.310 --> 34:02.260
You mean

519
34:02.500 --> 34:03.630
abandoning the original plan

520
34:03.630 --> 34:05.590
to link up with the 2nd and 6th Corps in western Hunan?

521
34:05.590 --> 34:06.500
Yes.

522
34:06.660 --> 34:08.060
Bo Gu and Li De's decision

523
34:08.350 --> 34:11.100
to head north to western Hunan may seem resolute,

524
34:11.159 --> 34:13.460
but it's fundamentally driven by flightism.

525
34:13.460 --> 34:15.040
They treat linking up with the 2nd and 6th Corps

526
34:15.040 --> 34:16.370
as their only lifeline,

527
34:16.540 --> 34:18.420
while completely disregarding the reality of the enemy's movements.

528
34:18.420 --> 34:19.820
If we keep heading north,

529
34:20.460 --> 34:22.860
western Hunan will be a second Xiang River.

530
34:22.889 --> 34:24.630
Why should we walk right into their trap?

531
34:24.630 --> 34:26.550
There are other paths we can take.

532
34:26.580 --> 34:27.790
Comrade Zedong,

533
34:28.020 --> 34:28.940
my only fear is

534
34:29.100 --> 34:30.300
that your suggestion

535
34:30.420 --> 34:32.580
won't be accepted by Bo Gu and Li De.

536
34:38.060 --> 34:40.100
This concerns the very survival of the Central Red Army.

537
34:40.100 --> 34:41.909
We cannot allow them to remain so stubborn.

538
34:41.909 --> 34:43.100
I'll go find Enlai right now

539
34:43.100 --> 34:44.310
and explain my views to him.

540
34:44.310 --> 34:45.620
Comrade Zedong,

541
34:46.500 --> 34:47.830
no need to look for me.

542
34:48.750 --> 34:50.270
I came to inform you

543
34:50.270 --> 34:51.020
to attend

544
34:51.020 --> 34:52.750
an emergency meeting of the Central Committee leaders

545
34:52.750 --> 34:54.500
to discuss our next move.

546
34:57.270 --> 34:58.200
Comrade Zedong,

547
34:58.310 --> 35:00.840
I hope you will speak your mind at the meeting.

548
35:01.020 --> 35:04.150
We'll make our decision after a collective discussion.

549
35:06.800 --> 35:07.560
Enlai,

550
35:07.780 --> 35:09.840
so you're willing to listen to me now?

551
35:10.460 --> 35:11.390
Of course we are.

552
35:11.940 --> 35:13.420
Since we left Yudu,

553
35:13.450 --> 35:15.020
you've come to us three times.

554
35:15.020 --> 35:16.310
I know it all.

555
35:16.750 --> 35:18.350
You've been wronged a lot,

556
35:18.830 --> 35:21.140
but I hope you won't take it to heart.

557
35:21.290 --> 35:23.170
Be brave and speak your mind.

558
35:23.370 --> 35:25.060
The Commander-in-Chief just told me

559
35:25.060 --> 35:25.980
at this critical moment,

560
35:25.980 --> 35:28.830
we need this cold pot of yours to give off steam.

561
35:29.620 --> 35:31.230
I've never been a cold pot.

562
35:31.540 --> 35:32.740
Enlai, rest assured.

563
35:32.820 --> 35:35.410
I will certainly do my part.

564
35:38.620 --> 35:39.850
Comrade Zedong,

565
35:40.670 --> 35:42.530
you washed your feet for nothing.

566
35:44.210 --> 35:45.670
I'll just wash them again.

567
35:46.550 --> 35:49.240
The Duke of Zhou paused his meals to welcome the wise,

568
35:49.240 --> 35:52.020
Today, Mao Runzhi greets Zhou Enlai with wet feet.

569
35:52.020 --> 35:54.280
The reason is the same: they are anxious.

570
35:54.420 --> 35:55.770
Military matters are urgent. Let's go.

571
35:55.770 --> 35:56.610
Let's move.

572
35:57.200 --> 35:57.920
Enlai.

573
35:59.350 --> 36:00.230
What about me?

574
36:00.420 --> 36:01.480
Get me a stretcher.

575
36:01.970 --> 36:03.000
We forgot about you.

576
36:03.000 --> 36:04.200
Come, I'll carry you.

577
36:04.540 --> 36:05.830
Slow down, slow down.

578
36:06.700 --> 36:07.960
I'm not wearing shoes!

579
36:08.350 --> 36:09.230
Why bother with shoes?

580
36:09.230 --> 36:10.490
You're stretching me.

581
36:10.790 --> 36:12.100
Comrade Zedong,

582
36:14.390 --> 36:16.390
this is the current situation.

583
36:16.670 --> 36:18.140
Things are highly critical.

584
36:18.140 --> 36:19.800
We have all just discussed it.

585
36:19.980 --> 36:21.620
Now let's ask Comrade Luofu,

586
36:21.920 --> 36:23.790
Comrade Jiaxiang, and Comrade Zedong

587
36:23.790 --> 36:25.420
to share your thoughts.

588
36:27.420 --> 36:28.580
I request to speak.

589
36:29.390 --> 36:31.980
Mao, you are a non-voting delegate.

590
36:35.430 --> 36:36.490
I request to speak.

591
36:36.620 --> 36:41.020
Comrade Zedong, please speak.

592
36:42.420 --> 36:45.100
I propose we march west into Guizhou.

593
36:45.630 --> 36:48.930
I propose we march west into Guizhou.

594
36:49.270 --> 36:51.830
There are two reasons to head west into Guizhou.

595
36:51.830 --> 36:52.870
First,

596
36:53.020 --> 36:54.870
from a practical perspective,

597
36:55.140 --> 36:56.580
the Guizhou Army's combat effectiveness

598
36:56.580 --> 36:59.790
is incomparable to that of the Hunan and Guangxi armies.

599
36:59.940 --> 37:02.420
Our Red 2nd and 6th Corps

600
37:02.670 --> 37:05.790
have repeatedly stated in telegrams to the Military Commission

601
37:05.790 --> 37:08.050
that the Guizhou Army has poor weaponry,

602
37:08.350 --> 37:10.060
lax discipline,

603
37:10.710 --> 37:12.230
and weak combat effectiveness.

604
37:12.230 --> 37:15.020
They even have serious internal conflicts.

605
37:15.470 --> 37:16.390
These are all

606
37:16.420 --> 37:18.620
favorable conditions for us in combat.

607
37:18.670 --> 37:22.330
Compared to the Hunan, Guangxi, and Central Armies

608
37:22.620 --> 37:24.980
Chiang Kai-shek has massed in western Hunan

609
37:24.980 --> 37:27.040
to form four blockade lines against us,

610
37:27.040 --> 37:29.520
the Guizhou Army's defense line

611
37:29.550 --> 37:30.620
around Liping and Jinping

612
37:30.620 --> 37:33.270
is obviously much easier to break through.

613
37:34.350 --> 37:35.230
Second,

614
37:35.390 --> 37:37.120
from a strategic perspective,

615
37:37.230 --> 37:39.060
if we head north to western Hunan,

616
37:39.060 --> 37:41.190
Chiang Kai-shek has already anticipated it.

617
37:41.190 --> 37:42.850
So he has mobilized his troops

618
37:42.980 --> 37:45.370
and set up several blockade lines against us.

619
37:45.370 --> 37:46.870
Marching west into Guizhou

620
37:46.870 --> 37:49.230
will completely disrupt his predictions.

621
37:49.230 --> 37:51.060
This is a surprise attack,

622
37:51.750 --> 37:53.080
catching him off guard.

623
37:53.460 --> 37:55.830
Chiang Kai-shek won't be able to

624
37:55.980 --> 37:58.670
redeploy his forces in the short term

625
37:58.670 --> 37:59.830
to encircle and suppress us.

626
37:59.830 --> 38:01.090
When we get to Guizhou,

627
38:01.100 --> 38:03.190
we can exploit the enemy's weaknesses.

628
38:03.190 --> 38:04.270
A few victories

629
38:04.700 --> 38:05.850
will allow our troops

630
38:05.850 --> 38:08.450
to quickly rest and refit.

631
38:08.860 --> 38:09.980
Exactly.

632
38:10.910 --> 38:12.230
Our corps have just fought

633
38:12.230 --> 38:14.020
the Battle of the Xiang River

634
38:14.750 --> 38:17.710
and marched hundreds of lis through the mountains of northern Guangxi.

635
38:17.710 --> 38:19.540
The men are exhausted,

636
38:19.910 --> 38:22.670
and our weapons and gear are depleted.

637
38:22.940 --> 38:25.140
We desperately need rest and resupply.

638
38:25.670 --> 38:26.730
Most importantly,

639
38:26.870 --> 38:28.190
we can seize

640
38:28.310 --> 38:29.830
the strategic initiative.

641
38:29.830 --> 38:30.870
When two armies clash,

642
38:30.870 --> 38:33.470
whoever gains the strategic initiative first

643
38:33.600 --> 38:35.060
will lead the enemy by the nose.

644
38:35.060 --> 38:37.310
Enough, enough!

645
38:37.540 --> 38:38.990
That's enough, Mao.

646
38:39.020 --> 38:39.870
I said enough!

647
38:40.110 --> 38:42.460
Let me emphasize this again.

648
38:42.530 --> 38:44.350
The plan to march north into western Hunan

649
38:44.350 --> 38:47.580
and join forces with the 2nd and 6th Corps

650
38:47.580 --> 38:50.870
will absolutely not change!

651
38:51.020 --> 38:54.310
Any other suggestion

652
38:54.540 --> 38:56.940
is a violation of

653
38:56.940 --> 39:01.540
the strategic direction approved by the Comintern,

654
39:01.540 --> 39:04.270
as well as a reckless and cowardly retreat.

655
39:06.500 --> 39:07.710
Comrade Li De,

656
39:07.910 --> 39:10.540
don't constantly use

657
39:10.760 --> 39:15.280
the Comintern's name to browbeat people.

658
39:23.190 --> 39:24.310
Comrade Li De,

659
39:24.760 --> 39:28.170
the Communist Party doesn't survive on intimidation.

660
39:29.360 --> 39:32.400
It thrives on the truth of Marxism-Leninism,

661
39:32.540 --> 39:34.380
on seeking truth from facts,

662
39:34.750 --> 39:36.270
and on a scientific approach.

663
39:36.270 --> 39:38.420
... truth and science.

664
39:38.670 --> 39:40.270
The Comintern does not understand

665
39:40.270 --> 39:41.790
our current predicament.

666
39:42.420 --> 39:43.710
How can they possibly

667
39:43.710 --> 39:45.840
provide us with scientific guidance?

668
39:45.980 --> 39:47.580
Putting everything else aside,

669
39:47.580 --> 39:49.390
given the current enemy situation,

670
39:49.390 --> 39:52.580
how can you prevent the Red Army from marching into

671
39:52.750 --> 39:54.810
the traps the enemy has already laid?

672
39:55.060 --> 39:56.540
Sticking to the original plan

673
39:56.540 --> 40:01.590
is risky!

674
40:17.060 --> 40:18.530
Our current task is...

675
40:19.000 --> 40:22.040
We can stay put for now.

676
40:22.310 --> 40:25.710
Let the enemies pursuing us along the main road

677
40:25.710 --> 40:29.110
overtake us first.

678
40:29.130 --> 40:32.340
Then suddenly swing north behind their backs,

679
40:33.100 --> 40:37.180
bypass their blockhouse lines,

680
40:37.210 --> 40:41.540
join the 2nd and 6th Corps,

681
40:41.620 --> 40:44.540
and then together develop a new Soviet base area.

682
40:44.870 --> 40:46.310
Comrade Li De,

683
40:46.780 --> 40:49.780
do you think our enemy is blind and deaf?

684
40:50.140 --> 40:51.870
We have tens of thousands of men.

685
40:51.870 --> 40:53.750
Will they just turn a blind eye?

686
40:53.990 --> 40:55.450
The blockhouses are dead,

687
40:55.710 --> 40:56.910
but the men are alive.

688
40:56.950 --> 40:58.240
We might bypass the blockhouses,

689
40:58.240 --> 41:00.550
but can we avoid 200,000 National Party?

690
41:00.580 --> 41:02.460
The enemy situation is constantly changing.

691
41:02.460 --> 41:03.190
Do the changes in the enemy situation

692
41:03.190 --> 41:04.620
bend to your will?

693
41:04.900 --> 41:05.790
Then tell me,

694
41:06.060 --> 41:08.540
how do we make the pursuing enemy overtake us first?

695
41:08.540 --> 41:09.580
Will the enemy take orders from you?

696
41:09.580 --> 41:11.540
The enemy situation is constantly changing.

697
41:11.540 --> 41:12.790
Didn't you hear me?

698
41:13.270 --> 41:14.530
Translate it for them!

699
41:14.910 --> 41:16.420
The enemy situation is constantly changing.

700
41:16.420 --> 41:17.230
Comrades,

701
41:19.230 --> 41:21.710
the Second Bureau just deciphered the enemy's latest deployment.

702
41:21.710 --> 41:23.510
You might all want to take a look.

703
41:23.590 --> 41:24.350
Comrade Xisheng!

704
41:24.350 --> 41:24.750
Here!

705
41:24.830 --> 41:25.540
Comrade Zhuangfei!

706
41:25.540 --> 41:26.060
Here!

707
41:26.100 --> 41:26.790
Come in.

708
41:27.060 --> 41:27.790
Commanders,

709
41:27.940 --> 41:29.200
this is what we just deciphered:

710
41:29.200 --> 41:30.620
the military deployment order

711
41:30.620 --> 41:33.280
from the enemy's frontline commander, Xue Yue.

712
41:34.710 --> 41:35.620
For your convenience,

713
41:35.620 --> 41:37.280
I added Russian annotations.

714
41:49.100 --> 41:51.270
Given the latest enemy situation,

715
41:51.580 --> 41:53.440
I fully agree with Mao's proposal

716
41:53.600 --> 41:55.160
to march west into Guizhou.

717
41:55.420 --> 41:58.080
I strongly support Comrade Zedong's proposal.

718
41:58.270 --> 42:00.870
I also agree with Comrade Mao Zedong's proposal.

719
42:00.870 --> 42:02.870
I agree with Mao Zedong's decision.

720
42:04.310 --> 42:05.870
Weighing the situation on both sides,

721
42:05.870 --> 42:08.540
our only option is to change our route of march

722
42:08.700 --> 42:09.870
and head west into Guizhou,

723
42:09.870 --> 42:12.140
so our field army can get some rest.

724
42:12.350 --> 42:14.020
Therefore, I believe

725
42:14.190 --> 42:16.320
Comrade Zedong's opinion is correct.

726
42:16.420 --> 42:18.030
Comrade Mao Zedong is right.

727
42:18.060 --> 42:18.910
Mao!

728
42:19.230 --> 42:21.460
You dismissed me so brutally!

729
42:22.620 --> 42:23.940
You dismissed me so brutally!

730
42:23.940 --> 42:26.500
Yet you, Zhou Enlai, actually side with him!

731
42:26.960 --> 42:29.420
Yet you, Zhou Enlai, actually side with him!

732
42:29.880 --> 42:31.630
Comrade Li De, I support...

733
42:31.750 --> 42:33.140
Comrade Li De! Comrade Li De!

734
42:33.140 --> 42:33.790
Comrade Li De!

735
42:33.790 --> 42:34.390
Careful!

736
42:36.460 --> 42:37.260
Comrade Li De!

737
42:37.350 --> 42:38.230
Comrade Li De!

738
42:38.780 --> 42:39.660
Comrade Li De!

739
42:39.790 --> 42:40.590
Comrade Li De!

740
42:40.790 --> 42:42.020
Take him back to rest.

741
42:42.390 --> 42:43.420
Comrade Li De.

742
42:44.670 --> 42:45.460
Watch out.

743
42:51.580 --> 42:51.940
Here.

744
42:52.270 --> 42:53.400
Here, Comrade Li De.

745
42:53.460 --> 42:54.790
Comrade Li De!

746
42:57.270 --> 42:58.420
Comrade Li De!

747
42:59.100 --> 43:00.140
Bo Gu.

748
43:01.100 --> 43:01.830
Listen to me.

749
43:02.390 --> 43:03.710
You must not waver.
